        {
          "name": "pqs:context",
          "value": "SHA-256 via Ruby's stdlib Digest — the only algorithm in this educational toy-bitcoin repo. Three shapes: (1) PoW mining loops hashing nonce-prefixed block data until leading zeros (blockchain.rb:20, timestamp.rb:13/27, block_with_proof_of_work.rb:18, hashrate.rb:8, block.rb:10); (2) demo prints of digests (hash.rb, block_with_proof_of_work.rb:48-58, the `==` verification lines); (3) Bitcoin's SHA256d block-header hash — double SHA-256 of the 80-byte serialized header in bitcoin_hash.rb:48-49/78"
